:: Fishing Combat Moor
<<effects>>
<<run fishingCombatEffects()>>
<<run fishingAttentionCheck()>>

/* Fishing gets interrupted by an attack */
<<if _fishingDangerEventTriggered>>
	<<fishCombatMoorAttackInterrupt $fishing.moor.event>>
<<else>>
	/* Player orgasm */
	<<if $arousal gte $arousalmax>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase is "watching">>
			<<fishCombatMoorOrgasmFox>>
		<<elseif ["sit", "campfire"].includes($daily.fishing.moor.hikers.phase)>>
			<<fishCombatMoorOrgasmHikers>>
		<<else>>
			<<fishCombatMoorOrgasm>>
		<</if>>

	/* You've caught the fish */
	<<elseif $fishing.combat.fishDistance lte 0>>
		<<if ["sit", "campfire"].includes($daily.fishing.moor.hikers.phase)>>
			<<fishCombatMoorCaughtHikers>>
		<<elseif $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase is "watching">>
			<<fishCombatMoorCaughtFox>>
		<<else>>
			<<fishCombatMoorCaught>>
		<</if>>

	/* Your line has snapped */
	<<elseif $fishing.combat.lineHealth lte 0>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase is "watching">>
			<<fishCombatMoorLineSnappedFox>>
		<<elseif ["sit", "campfire"].includes($daily.fishing.moor.hikers.phase) and !(playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant())>>
			<<fishCombatMoorLineSnappedHikers>>
		<<else>>
			<<fishCombatMoorLineSnapped>>
		<</if>>

	/* Fishing combat continues */
	<<else>>
		<<if $daily.fishing.moor.fox.phase is "watching">>
			<<fishCombatMoorMainFox>>
		<<else>>
			<<fishCombatMoorMain>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Cut Line
<<effects>>
<<run endFishingCombat()>>
You release the tension on the rod, letting the line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, the line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Combat Moor [widget]
<<widget "fishCombatMoorAttackInterrupt">>
	<<set $fishing.moor.event to "none">>
	<<set $fishing.moor.eventDanger to 0>>
	<<if _args[0] is "lurker">>
		<<include "Fishing Moor Lurker Interrupt Attack">>
	<<elseif _args[0] is "cat">>
		<<include "Fishing Moor Cat Interrupt Attack">>
	<<elseif _args[0] is "moorHikers">>
		<<include "Fishing Moor Hiker Interrupt Attack">>
	<<else>>
		<<error { message: "fishCombatMoorAttackInterrupt: unknown event value: " + _args[0] }>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorCaught">>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "moor")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<run holdCaughtFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "moor">>
	<br><br>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Moor Keep]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Moor Throw Back]]>><</link>>
	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Moor Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorMain">>
	<<run fishCombatAction()>>
	<<fishCombatActionDescription>>
	<<printFishInfo>>
	<br><br>

	<<fishCombatActions "Moor">>
	<<fishingMoorCombatDebugLinks>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorLineSnapped">>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> disappears into the depths.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatMoorOrgasm">>
	<<orgasmFishingMoor>>
	The rod slips from your grip. By the time you find your footing again, the line is slack and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
